#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# fourier_cos_series

#% text
# `fourier_cos_series(f, t, k)` gives the Fourier cosine series of `f` to order `k`: `a_0/2` plus `a_n cos(n t)` for `n` from 1 to `k`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The coefficients are those of `fourier_cos_coefficient` (from the half period `[0, pi]`); `fourier_parameters: [a, b]` scales the frequency by `b`.

#% item
# Lists of variables and orders give the series in products of cosines.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
fourier_cos_series(t^2, t, 3)
#% output
#= cos(2*t) - 4*cos(t) - (4/9)*cos(3*t) + (1/3)*pi^2

#% cell
fourier_cos_series(abs(t), t, 3)
#% output
#= (1/2)*pi - 4*cos(t)/pi - 4*cos(3*t)/(9*pi)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `fourier_sin_series`, `fourier_trig_series`, `fourier_cos_coefficient`
